<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <title>Slack Invite Automation: Help</title>
  <%= partial 'public/partials/_head.html.erb' %>
</head>
<body class="site-page">
  <%= partial 'public/partials/_navigation.html.erb' %>
  <main id="main" class="page-container content-page">
    <h1>A little help getting people in.</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">Set up your team's join page, choose how invitations work, and welcome your next member.</p>
    <section class="help-section" aria-labelledby="start-title">
      <h2 id="start-title">Your first invitation</h2>
      <ol class="getting-started">
        <li>Add Slack Invite Automation to your Slack team.</li>
        <li>Follow the bot's instructions to authorize an admin to send invitations.</li>
        <li>Share your public join page so people can request an invitation with their name and email.</li>
      </ol>
      <%= partial 'public/partials/_install_button.html.erb' %>
    </section>
    <section class="help-section" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
      <h2 id="questions-title">Setup &amp; questions</h2>
      <details class="help-topic">
        <summary>How do I authorize invitations?</summary>
        <p>The bot asks a Slack admin to authorize it to send invitations on their behalf. Follow the authorization link supplied by the bot.</p>
        <img src="<%= h asset_path('/img/authorize.png') %>" width="910" height="290" alt="Slack inviting an admin to authorize invitation sending" loading="lazy">
      </details>
      <details class="help-topic">
        <summary>What do people see when they join?</summary>
        <p>Your public page shows your team's name, icon, and Slack address. Visitors enter their name and email; after the invitation is sent, Slack emails them a link to join.</p>
        <img class="invitation-preview" src="<%= h asset_path('/img/invite.png') %>" width="1600" height="1000" alt="The public Slack invitation form" loading="lazy">
        <img src="<%= h asset_path('/img/email.png') %>" width="1284" height="744" alt="An email invitation to join a Slack team" loading="lazy">
      </details>
      <details class="help-topic">
        <summary>Can an admin approve each request?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Send <code>set approval on</code> to the bot. Slack admins are DMed join requests, which they can approve or ignore.</p>
        <img src="<%= h asset_path('/img/approval.png') %>" width="948" height="212" alt="Enabling administrative approval" loading="lazy">
        <img src="<%= h asset_path('/img/join.png') %>" width="982" height="198" alt="An admin reviewing an invitation request in Slack" loading="lazy">
      </details>
      <details class="help-topic">
        <summary>Can I change who sends invitations?</summary>
        <p>Send <code>set sender @username</code> to choose the Slack admin sending invitations. The selected admin must authorize the bot.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="help-topic">
        <summary>Where can I find more commands?</summary>
        <p>DM <code>help</code> to <code>@invite</code> for more commands, settings, and subscription information.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="help-topic">
        <summary>How much does it cost?</summary>
        <p>You can try the bot free for two weeks without a credit card. After that, a subscription costs $9.99 per Slack team per year and automatically renews.</p>
      </details>
    </section>
    <section id="support" class="help-section">
      <h2>Still need a hand?</h2>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/vestris/slack-invite/issues/new">Open a GitHub issue</a>, contact <a href="https://twitter.com/playplayio">@playplayio</a>, or email <a href="mailto:dblock@vestris.com">dblock@vestris.com</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <%= partial 'public/partials/_footer.html.erb' %>
</body>
</html>
